{
  "$schema": "../family.schema.json",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "dip",
  "name": "Dip",
  "definition": "A strict bilateral closed-chain compound push performed while the hands remain on selected fixed handles or independent rings. The bodyweight branches suspend the full body; the exact Life Fitness Pro 2 PSADC branch supports the knees on a guided assistance pad and subtracts the selected assistance from bodyweight. From a conditioned bottom position with the shoulders extended behind anatomical neutral and the elbows flexed, the concentric phase returns the shoulders only toward neutral through shoulder flexion while extending the elbows. Parallel-bar sternocostal-site EMG and measured bar/ring kinematics support the muscle and action contract. The PSADC manual directly defines its adjustable lower handles, knee-pad assistance, and controlled elbow raising and lowering; assigning the conditioned shoulder path and muscle roles to that fixture is a disclosed mechanics transfer rather than a manual measurement. Other assisted machines, band-assisted, bench-supported, standing-assisted, kipping, and transition variants remain outside this contract.",
  "evidenceRefs": [
    "ackland-2008-shoulder-moment-arms",
    "cinarli-2021-parallel-bar-dip",
    "da-silva-2022-ring-dip-pectoralis-rupture",
    "mckenzie-2022-dip-variations",
    "mckenzie-2022-bar-dip-fatigue",
    "life-fitness-2007-pro2-series-manual"
  ],
